    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d560">

                <pb facs="0982" n="886" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg886"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">853.51/303: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-12-11T00:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 11,
                                1925—midnight</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received December 12—6:15
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>45. Foreign Minister asks to be informed how many Tobacco Bonds are held by
                    Americans, their value in sterling and where deposited. <pb facs="0983" n="887"
                        xml:id="pg887"/> Have pointedly called his attention to last two sentences
                    Department’s instruction number 6, February 7, 7 p.m., but said I would inquire
                    again by telegraph. Please reply by telegraph.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d560-f1"
                    /></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d560-f1" n="12" xml:id="d560-f1-content">
                <p>The Department referred the Minister to its telegram No. 6, Feb. 7, 1925, 7 p.m.,
                        <ref target="#pg883">p. 883</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
